# Day 3 – Learning Notes

## Objectives Achieved

* Understood the differences between Validation Rules, Flows, and Apex Triggers.
* Learned when to use declarative automation instead of Apex.
* Built a Record-Triggered Flow to automate business processes.
* Automatically populated the Application Date when a new Application was created.
* Created Validation Rules to improve data quality.
* Learned how Before-Save and After-Save Flows work.
* Understood how different automation tools work together in Salesforce.

## Features Implemented

* Record-Triggered Flow for automatically setting the Application Date.
* Validation Rules for business rule enforcement.
* Enhanced the Placement Management System with declarative automation.
* Explored automatic Offer Letter creation using Flow.

## Key Concepts Learned

* Validation Rules
* Record-Triggered Flow
* Before-Save Flow
* Flow Builder
* Declarative Automation
* Automation Best Practices

## Outcome

Successfully implemented declarative automation using Flow and Validation Rules, reducing the need for Apex wherever possible while improving the Placement Management System.
